@startuml Sequence_Approval_Workflow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Award Approval Workflow Sequence Diagram

actor "Reviewer\n(any level)" as reviewer
actor "Owner" as owner
participant "Web Application" as webapp
participant "ReviewController" as api
participant "BatchReview" as batch
participant "ReviewAssignment" as assignment
participant "ReviewDecisions" as decisions
participant "Transitions" as transitions
database "PostgreSQL" as db
participant "DecisionMails\n(after commit)" as mails

note over webapp, db
    Steps are the same at every level (faculty secretary, dean,
    rector's secretary, rector); the level only changes who may
    review (role or delegation scope) and whether an approval is final.
    Batch decisions (4.1.4) run the same decision per request,
    each in its own transaction.
end note

== Queue and claim (4.1.1) ==
reviewer -> webapp: Open "На розгляді"
webapp -> api: GET /api/v1/reviews?assigned=…&level=…
api -> db: open requests at the caller's levels and scopes
api --> webapp: page of ReviewItem
reviewer -> webapp: Open the award
webapp -> api: GET /api/v1/awards/{id}/reviewer
api --> webapp: ReviewItem (holder, deadline, version)

opt Claim before deciding
    reviewer -> webapp: «Взяти в роботу»
    webapp -> api: PUT /awards/{id}/reviewer {requestVersion}
    api -> assignment: claim
    assignment -> db: SELECT … FOR UPDATE, check version
    assignment -> db: status IN_REVIEW, current_reviewer_id
    api --> webapp: ReviewItem
end

== Decision (4.1.2) ==
reviewer -> webapp: «Затвердити» / «Повернути» / «Відхилити» / «Передати …»
webapp -> webapp: dialog: comment (required for return and reject),\n«Документи перевірено» on approval
webapp -> api: POST /awards/{id}/decisions\n{decision, requestVersion, comment?, verified?}
api -> decisions: decide
decisions -> db: SELECT … FOR UPDATE
alt held by a colleague / stale version / already decided
    decisions --> api: 409 request-claimed | request-stale | request-closed
    api --> webapp: problem
    webapp --> reviewer: notice, panel read again
else open request
    decisions -> transitions: next state (level, category minimum)
    transitions --> decisions: APPROVED | ESCALATED (next level not passed over)\n| RETURNED | REJECTED
    decisions -> db: UPDATE award_requests (status, level,\nreviewer, deadline, version)
    decisions -> db: UPDATE awards (status, verification_badge)
    decisions -> db: INSERT review_decisions (delegator_id)
    decisions -> db: INSERT award_versions (DECIDED), audit_logs (REVIEW_DECISION)
    decisions --> api: DecisionOutcome
    api --> webapp: 200 {status, requestStatus, level, requestVersion}
    webapp --> reviewer: «Нагороду затверджено» / «Передано декану» …,\nstatus and timeline reloaded
    decisions -> mails: decision event, delivered after the commit
    mails -> owner: e-mail: approved, passed on, returned\nwith the comment or rejected with the reason
end

== Batch decision (4.1.4) ==
reviewer -> webapp: select rows, «Затвердити (n)» / «Повернути» / …
webapp -> api: GET /reviews/templates?decision=…
api --> webapp: templates in the caller's language
webapp -> webapp: dialog: «Шаблон відповіді» fills the comment
webapp -> batch: POST /reviews/decisions\n{decision, comment?, items[{awardId, requestVersion}]}
batch -> batch: 1–50 distinct items (400), comment (422)
loop every item, in the order sent
    batch -> decisions: decide (own transaction)
    alt decided
        decisions --> batch: DecisionOutcome → DONE
        decisions -> mails: decision event, after that item's commit
    else 404 / 409 / 422
        decisions --> batch: problem → FAILED {code, detail}
    end
end
batch -> db: INSERT audit_logs (REVIEW_BATCH: items, done, failed)
batch --> webapp: 200 [ {awardId, outcome, code?, status?, level?} ]
webapp --> reviewer: «Опрацьовано: n з m», failed awards with reasons;\ndecided rows leave the queue, failed stay selected

== Owner ==
owner -> webapp: Open the award
webapp -> api: GET /awards/{id}/status
api --> webapp: path (DONE, SKIPPED, CURRENT, UPCOMING),\ndecisions with reviewer, delegator and comment

@enduml
